---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageFrame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro';
import WorkSection from '../components/WorkSection.astro';
import ActionRow from '../components/ActionRow.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import Dot from '../components/Dot.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Carousel from '../components/Carousel.astro';
import CaseLead from '../components/CaseLead.astro';
import MetaLine from '../components/MetaLine.astro';
const head = `<link rel="icon" href="data:," />`;
const afterFooter = ``;
---
<Base title={"Design work - Gorka Molero"} description={"These are screens Gorka Molero designed for four of his products."} page="design-work">
  <Fragment slot="head" set:html={head} />
  <PageFrame class="sheet">
    <Masthead />

      <CaseLead class="lead">
        <MetaLine class="meta eyebrow">2026 &middot; Product interfaces</MetaLine>
        <h2 class="case-title">Design work</h2>
        <p class="intro">I design what I build. Here are screens from four of my products.</p>
      </CaseLead>

      <main class="systems">
      <WorkSection class="work" id="the-pulse">
        <h2><a href="./the-pulse.html">The Pulse</a></h2>
        <MetaLine class="meta">Own project &middot; 2025&ndash;2026 <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> Live at <a href="https://the-pulse.games" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the-pulse.games</a></MetaLine>
        <p>The Pulse is a set of live AI-narrated interactive stories you play by voice.</p>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/pulse-home.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/pulse-home.webp" width="2560" height="1600" loading="lazy" alt="The Pulse home page: five tall panels side by side, each with an engraving-style illustration, a Roman numeral, the story's title in spaced serif capitals and its genre." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>Each story gets a tall panel with its own illustration.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/pulse-home-hover.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/pulse-home-hover.webp" width="2560" height="1600" loading="lazy" alt="The Pulse home page with the Shadow Over Innsmouth panel widened and tinted green, showing its blurb and a Begin link, while the other four panels stay dark." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>On hover, a story's panel widens and takes on its colour.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate narrow">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/pulse-story-card.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/pulse-story-card.webp" width="1240" height="1800" loading="lazy" alt="The story card for Shadow Over Innsmouth: the title over a faint illustration, a Lovecraft epigraph, the premise, and a list of ways to play, Solo, Same Screen and Invite Room, with Narration on." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>Each story opens on a card with three ways to play.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/pulse-chat.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/pulse-chat.webp" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="A story in play: serif narration in a column on the left, the player's lines right-aligned in a sans, a generated image of the stationmaster with a lantern on the right, and a What do you do? box at the bottom." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>In play, the scene's image sits beside the narration.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate narrow">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/pulse-phone.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/pulse-phone.webp" width="1170" height="2532" loading="lazy" alt="The Pulse home page on a phone: the five stories as a stack of wide bands with their titles over the illustrations." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>On a phone, the panels stack into bands.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button" href="./the-pulse.html">The case study</TextLink>
          <TextLink class="button" href="https://the-pulse.games">Open the-pulse.games</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work" id="hotpress">
        <h2><a href="./hotpress.html">Hotpress</a></h2>
        <MetaLine class="meta">Own project &middot; 2026 <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> Live at <a href="https://hotpress.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">hotpress.app</a></MetaLine>
        <p>Hotpress is an app for writing together in real time, with print-ready book and e-book export. I gave it a neobrutalist look, with heavy black borders and hard shadows.</p>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/hotpress-dashboard.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/hotpress-dashboard.webp" width="2360" height="740" loading="lazy" alt="The Hotpress projects dashboard: Your Projects with a yellow New Project button and three black-bordered project cards topped by red and blue rules, each with a hard black shadow." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>Projects sit on black-bordered cards with a coloured rule on top.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/hotpress-editor-preview.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/hotpress-editor-preview.webp" width="2880" height="1736" loading="lazy" alt="The Hotpress editor with a manuscript, The House of Tides, and the PDF Preview panel beside it showing a typeset 6 by 9 inch page in EB Garamond with drop caps and a centred scene break." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>The print preview shows the book as it will print.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/hotpress-template-gallery.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/hotpress-template-gallery.webp" width="2880" height="1180" loading="lazy" alt="The Choose a Template gallery: typeset sample pages for Ashford, Pemberton, Thornbury, Whitmore, Cambridge and Hawthorne with their fonts named underneath, with the Serif filter selected among All, Serif, Sans, Script, Genre-Specific and Accessible." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>The gallery shows each of the 22 templates as a typeset page.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/hotpress-format-typography.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/hotpress-format-typography.webp" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" alt="Hotpress Format Settings with the Typography section open: body font EB Garamond and heading font Playfair Display shown in their own typefaces, size and line height, and a preview of Chapter One, with Chapters, Page Layout and more sections below." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>Font menus show each typeface in its own letterforms.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button" href="./hotpress.html">The case study and the video</TextLink>
          <TextLink class="button" href="https://hotpress.app">Open hotpress.app</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work" id="koda">
        <h2><a href="./koda.html">Koda</a></h2>
        <MetaLine class="meta">Own project &middot; 2026 <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> Desktop app</MetaLine>
        <p>Koda is a desktop app for working collaboratively with coding agents. I gave it the look of a terminal.</p>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/koda-two-macs.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/koda-two-macs.webp" width="3200" height="1786" loading="lazy" alt="One Koda session on two Macs side by side: Gorka's window in the black Obsidian theme and Alex's in the blue-grey Graphite theme, both showing the same agent transcript, with SHARED BY GORKA · CONTROL on Alex's window." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>Here one session runs on two Macs, in two themes.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate narrow">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/koda-empty-session.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/koda-empty-session.webp" width="700" height="480" loading="lazy" alt="The KODA TERMINAL v0.1.0 box with the KODA mark drawn in ASCII block characters and Ready for input, above Type a message or use /commands." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>An empty session opens on the KODA mark in ASCII.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/koda-settings-themes.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/koda-settings-themes.webp" width="1440" height="525" loading="lazy" alt="Koda settings: a [THEME] section with four built-in theme cards, KODA Obsidian selected, Codex Light, KODA Dim and KODA Graphite, and an Import VS Code Theme button." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>It has four themes, and any VS Code theme can be imported.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/koda-share-dialog.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/koda-share-dialog.webp" width="1200" height="660" loading="lazy" alt="Koda's Share Workspace dialog: a thin frame with the title between corner marks, the invitation link in a field, and one footer row with [ESC] CLOSE on the left and [ DONE ] on the right." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>Dialogs are terminal frames with actions in brackets.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button" href="./koda.html">The case study and the video</TextLink>
          <TextLink class="button" href="https://gorkamolero.github.io/koda/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Koda's Storybook</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work" id="openroadie">
        <h2><a href="https://github.com/RoadieHQ/openroadie" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>openroadie</em></a></h2>
        <MetaLine class="meta"><a href="https://roadie.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Roadie</a> &middot; 2026 <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> Open source</MetaLine>
        <p><em>openroadie</em> is the open-source context layer that came out of Roadie, and I designed and built its interfaces. They run on <code>@roadiehq/ui</code>, a design system I co-led.</p>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/openroadie-pipeline-editor.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/openroadie-pipeline-editor.webp" width="2560" height="1600" loading="lazy" alt="The openroadie pipeline editor in the dark theme for a GitHub teams data source: schedule, source, two chained sources and store as cards joined by arrows, and after a dry run the selected step's JSON output in the panel on the right." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>A pipeline is a column of step cards, with each step's output beside it.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/openroadie-relationships-map.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/openroadie-relationships-map.webp" width="2560" height="1600" loading="lazy" alt="The openroadie relationships map in the dark theme, built with React Flow: nineteen data sources from GitHub, Okta, PagerDuty and Slack as cards with their join fields, linked by coloured and dashed lines, with a legend of relationship types and a minimap." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>The relationship map links data sources field to field.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/openroadie-onboarding-checklist.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/openroadie-onboarding-checklist.webp" width="2560" height="1600" loading="lazy" alt="The openroadie Getting started checklist in the light theme: a progress bar at four of six, the first four steps struck through as done, and a filled Create a context group button on the next step." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>The in-app checklist strikes off what's done.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button" href="https://github.com/RoadieHQ/openroadie">The source on GitHub</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>

      <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button primary" href="./design-systems.html">Design systems</TextLink>
        <TextLink class="button" href="./index.html">Engineering portfolio</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </main>
  </PageFrame>
  <Fragment slot="after-footer" set:html={afterFooter} />
</Base>
